{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"write-equipment-purchase-case","kind":"prompt","title":"Write a lab equipment purchase case","description":"Writes the case for buying a lab instrument, comparing options on specification, total cost of ownership, usage and alternatives such as core facilities, for a department or funder decision.","category":"lab-work","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan"],"role":["researcher","operations-manager"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["text","document"],"output":["docs","table"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"standard","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"intermediate","tags":["equipment-purchase","business-case","total-cost-of-ownership","instrument-quotes","core-facility"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["estimate-experiment-reagent-costs","set-up-equipment-booking-rules","plan-instrument-calibration-schedule"],"personas":["lab-manager"]},"args":[{"name":"need","description":"What the instrument is for, who would use it, how often, and what you do now without it (outsourcing, a core facility, borrowing).","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"options","description":"The instruments or quotes you are comparing, with prices, specifications, service contracts, consumables and installation needs as quoted.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"audience","description":"Who decides and what they care about, for example \"department equipment committee, needs shared use\" or \"grant equipment line\". Optional.","type":"text"}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["Summary","Need and users","Options compared","Total cost of ownership","Alternatives considered","Risks and requirements","Recommendation"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nEquipment committees reject cases that only show the purchase price and a wish list. They want evidence of use (hours per week, how many groups), a fair comparison against renting time at a core facility or outsourcing, and the full cost over the instrument's life: service contracts after warranty, proprietary consumables, software licences, installation (power, bench space, gases, ventilation), training and the staff time to run it. A specification that matches the actual experiments beats the top model, and shared use usually strengthens a case.\n</context>\n\n<task>\n<need>\n{{need}}\n</need>\n\n<options>\n{{options}}\n</options>\n{{#audience}}\n\n<audience>\n{{audience}}\n</audience>\n{{/audience}}\n\n1. Summary: the request, the cost and the recommended option in three sentences.\n2. Need and users: experiments it enables, expected usage, groups and projects, and what happens without it.\n3. Options compared: a table of the key specifications that matter for the stated experiments, not every specification.\n4. Total cost of ownership over a stated period (for example five years): purchase, installation, service after warranty, consumables, software, training, staff time. Use only the quoted figures; mark gaps.\n5. Alternatives considered: core facility time, outsourcing, refurbished or shared purchase, with their costs if given and their trade-offs (turnaround, access, data control).\n6. Risks and requirements: site requirements, who maintains it, booking rules, end-of-life.\n7. Recommendation with conditions (for example \"subject to confirming the service quote\").\n</task>\n\n<constraints>\n- Use only the prices and specifications provided; never invent a quote, a model name or a feature. Missing numbers are marked \"to obtain\".\n- Do not overstate usage; if usage is an estimate, say so and how it was estimated.\n- Keep vendor comparisons factual and based on the quotes.\n</constraints>\n\n<output_format>\n## Summary\n## Need and users\n## Options compared\n| Criterion | Option A | Option B |\n## Total cost of ownership\n| Cost item | Option A | Option B |\n## Alternatives considered\n## Risks and requirements\n## Recommendation\n</output_format>","steps":[]}
